Expected elements: present

All backbone is drawn: fixed nav, breadcrumb `Home / demo / tx / 0x27a6…9a6c`, footer with product line, three links, correct disclosure, and all three marks (solid text-coloured heart, CodeTracer, labelled GitHub). Exactly one provenance marker — the `Data` row form, `Synthetic demo data`, correct for a synthetic tree. No Debug button, no disabled control, no empty panel. All five iteration changes landed: Age, Type and the bordered hash box with its `click to select` caption are present; the provenance note now sets flush-left at a ~65-character measure and is the best-set prose on the page; cost is base ten (`42000 / 100000 mana (FeeJuice)`); the decoded-input note names the unknown-selector-plus-empty-calldata case truthfully; the `/demo` URL is live.

Typographically the page is competent but its top two levels collapse. The H1 (506,247) is ~29px mono at regular weight; the six section headings (e.g. Events at 506,1693) are ~24px bold sans — 1.19× smaller in cap height but heavier, so six level-two headings out-shout the single title across 2818px.

The new rows caused two side effects: `AGE`'s 22-character English statement is set in the letterspaced mono chip reserved for tokens like `Yes`/`Pending`, and `TYPE` is plain mono while the identically categorical `CANONICAL`/`FINALITY` are chipped.

Highest-priority fixes: separate H1 from the section level by weight or size; give the Age statement a prose treatment, not a token's.

Rating: 6/10

